    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<p><em>“You hum the frequency where killing each other feels wrong.”</em></p><p>Once per <strong>a Soma Break</strong>, you can spend an <strong>action</strong> to establish a brief field of enforced hesitation.</p><ul><li>You create a <strong>3 squares-radius aura</strong> centered on you that lasts for <strong>1 minute</strong> and moves with you.</li><li>Hostile creatures in the aura have <strong>disadvantage</strong> on attack rolls against creatures who have not made an attack since the start of their last turn (non-hostiles, negotiators, civilians, etc.).</li><li>Allies in the aura have <strong>reroll the lowest die on defense checks</strong> to end the <strong>charmed</strong> or <strong>Shaken</strong> conditions.</li></ul><p><em>The world doesn’t stop being dangerous. It just remembers, briefly, that it could be kind.</em></p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
